{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790420271506,"sessionID":"ses_f22a320d7ffeQcQJvEQv7gZZrl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9a1d49dca2264788be5c0130","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/task_config.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/task_config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"instruction\": \"In `scenes/world.tscn`, add a TileSet custom data layer named `tile_type` with type int, and assign GradientTexture1D exports named `water_color`, `dirt_color`, and `grass_color` on the World node. In `scripts/world.gd`, add `enum TILE_TYPES { NONE, WATER, DIRT, GRASS }`, export the three GradientTexture1D variables (`water_color`, `dirt_color`, `grass_color`), create a dictionary mapping TILE_TYPES to those gradients, and add a static `get_gradient_at(position)` that reads `get_custom_data_at(position, \\\"tile_type\\\")` and returns the matching gradient. In `scenes/tank.tscn`, add `LeftTrackParticles` and `RightTrackParticles` GPUParticles2D nodes with a ParticleProcessMaterial using box emission (emission_shape box) and `emission_box_extents.x = -16`, direction.y = -16 for left and +16 for right, spread 25, gravity = Vector3.ZERO, initial_velocity_max 4, damping_max 3, scale_min 0.25, amount 128, z_index -1, and `emitting = false`. In `scripts/tank.gd`, track the current particle gradient using `World.get_gradient_at(position)`, assign it to each emitter\\u2019s `process_material.color_ramp`, set both emitters to `emitting = true` while moving, and `emitting = false` when not moving.\"\n3: }\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"In `scenes/world.tscn`, add a TileSet custom data layer named `tile_type` with type int, and assign GradientTexture1D exports named `water_color`, `dirt_color`, and `grass_color` on the World node. In `scripts/world.gd`, add `enum TILE_TYPES { NONE, WATER, DIRT, GRASS }`, export the three GradientTexture1D variables (`water_color`